00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:15.120
JohnFx was wondering:
What are black holes spinning relative to?

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:19.280
Right, motion is relative, so you have to assign the coordinates to someone.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.920
In the case of black holes, that’s usually a distant inertial observer.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:26.000
It’s not always explicitly stated, but it is the standard.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.780
Anyway, thanks for watching!

